    "captions_text": "1\n00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,140\nRest is not the opposite of faithfulness. Sometimes it is what allows\n\n2\n00:00:03,140 --> 00:00:05,620\nus to return to it, but there is a difference between setting\n\n3\n00:00:05,620 --> 00:00:08,280\ndown a burden for a while and pretending it no longer belongs\n\n4\n00:00:08,280 --> 00:00:11,340\nto us. Tonight, we do not need to solve everything. We can\n\n5\n00:00:11,340 --> 00:00:13,760\nname one thing that is ours to do, one limit that deserves\n\n6\n00:00:13,760 --> 00:00:17,120\nrespect and one outcome we cannot control. Our worth is not a\n\n7\n00:00:17,120 --> 00:00:20,540\nscore measured by how many tasks we finish before we sleep. Consider\n\n8\n00:00:20,540 --> 00:00:24,000\na conversation you have been avoiding. Rest may help you return to\n\n9\n00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:26,460\nit with more patience. It does not make the other person or\n\n10\n00:00:26,460 --> 00:00:30,340\nthe issue disappear. Now consider a problem you cannot fix tonight. Continuing\n\n11\n00:00:30,340 --> 00:00:33,700\nto rehearse it is not the same as taking responsibility. These are\n\n12\n00:00:33,700 --> 00:00:37,040\nexamples to reflect on not diagnosis of your life. Some people need\n\n13\n00:00:37,040 --> 00:00:40,020\nto stop for longer. Their next honest step may be asking for\n\n14\n00:00:40,020 --> 00:00:43,440\nhelp or respecting a limit, not doing more, from this Christian perspective.\n\n15\n00:00:44,280 --> 00:00:47,820\nRest and responsibility need not compete. Choose a small response for later\n\n16\n00:00:47,820 --> 00:00:51,400\nwithout making this moment another demand. This is the perspective we offer.\n\n17\n00:00:51,760 --> 00:00:54,660\nRest can make room for a faithful response without becoming an excuse\n\n18\n00:00:54,660 --> 00:00:58,340\nfor avoidance. After these opening words, the speech will stop. The original\n\n19\n00:00:58,340 --> 00:01:02,040\nmusic will leave space for your own prayer, reflection, or quiet. You\n\n20\n00:01:02,040 --> 00:01:04,360\ndo not need to earn that space by staying here for the\n\n21\n00:01:04,360 --> 00:01:04,820\nwhole session.\n",
